The repository provides integration adapters for independently distributed
models and software. Their source code, checkpoints and datasets are not
vendored and are not relicensed by this project. Users must obtain them from
their official sources and comply with the corresponding terms.

Documented external projects include LLaVA, InternVL, Qwen-VL,
LLaVA-OneVision, GLM-4V, UNIAA, ArtiMuse, UniPercept, Aes-R1, ArtQuant,
AesExpert, Q-SiT, Q-Align/OneAlign, Hugging Face Transformers,
SentenceTransformers, BERTScore and pycocoevalcap/SPICE.

LLaVA is distributed under Apache License 2.0 in the audited upstream checkout.
Q-Align/OneAlign uses the S-Lab License 1.0, which restricts commercial use;
this repository only imports a separately installed copy and does not vendor
Q-Align source or weights. For projects whose local snapshot did not include a
license file, this release publishes only the independently written adapter and
requires users to verify the upstream terms before use.

Dataset annotations, images, prompt examples and model-generated predictions
are not distributed in this release. Dataset preparation scripts do not grant
redistribution rights.
